      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Clinical Case Study: Claire Miller**\n\n*Age:* 34\n*Occupation:* Office Manager\n\n*Chief Complaint:*\nClaire Miller presents to the emergency room with severe, constant abdominal pain that started approximately 6 hours prior.\n\n*History of Present Illness:*\nMs. Miller reports a sharp pain in her lower abdomen, localized around the midsection. She describes the pain as a gnawing sensation that intensifies when she moves or coughs. No associated fever but states that the pain disrupts her ability to concentrate on work. She denies any recent history of abdominal surgery, medical trauma, or similar episodes. Ms. Miller has not taken any medications for the pain, out of concern for masking a serious condition.\n\n*Review of Systems:*\nMs. Miller reports nausea but no vomiting. She denies diarrhea and has not experienced any change in bowel movements. She reports no urinary symptoms. She states that her dietary habits have not changed significantly and that she is still recovering from stress related to personal issues.\n\n*Vital Signs upon Admission:*\n- Temperature: 98.6°F (37°C)\n- Blood Pressure: 130/85 mmHg\n- Heart Rate: 98 bpm\n- Respiratory Rate: 18 breaths/min",
